package card

const experienceHTML = `{{define "experience"}}
<section id="experience"><div class="section-heading"><span class="index">Client experience / observed behavior</span><h2>Successful work, shedding and the long tail</h2></div>
<p class="lead">{{.ClientBehavior}}</p>
<div class="findings experience-headlines">
<article><span class="eyebrow">HTTP 429 / dispatched requests</span>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<h3>{{n (percent .http429 .dispatched) 1}}% <small>/ {{n .shares 0}} shares</small></h3>{{end}}<p>Whole-arm logical requests, not wire HTTP attempts or offers.</p></article>
<article><span class="eyebrow">Successful bodies / entire case</span>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<h3>{{n .successfulQPSWallIncludingDrain 2}} QPS <small>/ {{n .shares 0}} shares</small></h3>{{end}}<p>Total successful completions / elapsed API time including drain. Duration-weighted, not a mean of bin rates.</p></article>
<article><span class="eyebrow">Successful LIST p95</span>{{range .Card.apfComparison.arms}}<h3>{{n .successfulLISTP95Seconds 2}}s <small>/ {{n .shares 0}} shares</small></h3>{{end}}<p>Body-inclusive successful latency; rejected and timed-out requests excluded. Client request/body timeout: {{n .Card.apfComparison.client.requestTimeoutSeconds 0}}s, not an SLO.</p></article>
</div>
<p class="annotation">Small is a proposed resource profile, not a qualified client-capacity envelope. {{if .LimitedArms}}Generator limits reduced dispatched demand in this comparison; low successful throughput is an observed result, not an APF capacity estimate.{{else}}Client capacity cannot be established from resource requests alone.{{end}}</p>
{{if .Experience}}
<p class="muted">{{utc .Experience.window.start}} to {{utc .Experience.window.end}} UTC. All plots share this clock. Shaded arms identify APF shares, not QPS: configured demand is {{range .Experience.arms}}{{n .offeredQPS 0}} QPS at {{n .shares 0}} shares; {{end}}no observations are inferred between arms.</p>
<div class="experience-legend" aria-label="Arm and timing legend">{{range $i, $arm := .Experience.arms}}<span style="border-color:{{if eq $i 0}}#08796f{{else}}#687bc1{{end}}">{{n .shares 0}} shares: shaded active client window</span>{{end}}<span>Solid vertical: clients start</span><span>Dashed vertical: scheduling stops</span><span>Dotted vertical: API drain ends</span></div>
<figure><h3>Successful throughput over time</h3><div class="experience-controls"><label><input id="experience-total-toggle" type="checkbox"> Show all terminal completions, including HTTP 429 (gray dashed)</label></div><div id="experience-throughput" class="experience-plot" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Successful throughput timeline, scroll horizontally"></div><figcaption>Teal: successful body-complete QPS. Periwinkle dashed: Target Offered QPS, configured demand during active scheduling, then zero during drain. Each step spans its actual completion bin; drain completions may exceed target rate. No measured per-bin offers are available.</figcaption></figure>
<figure><h3>HTTP 429 fraction over time</h3><div id="experience-rejections" class="experience-plot" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="HTTP 429 percentage timeline, scroll horizontally"></div><figcaption>Orange: HTTP 429 / <strong>all completed requests in the bin</strong>, including terminal errors, on a 0-100% axis. Denominator is neither offers nor HTTP attempts. A null fraction is a gap, never 0%.</figcaption></figure>
<figure><h3>Successful GET and LIST tail latency over time</h3><div class="experience-controls"><label><input id="experience-outcome-toggle" type="checkbox"> Show all-outcome p95 (gray dashed)</label><label><input id="experience-timeout-toggle" type="checkbox"> Show client request/body timeout reference (not an SLO)</label></div><div id="experience-latency" class="experience-plot" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Successful latency timeline, scroll horizontally"></div><figcaption>Teal: successful GET p95. Periwinkle: successful LIST p95. Points are recorded raw nearest-rank quantiles at bin centers, not calculated from other quantiles. Fast rejections can hide successful tails in all-outcome p95, so it is off by default.</figcaption></figure>
<p class="muted">10-second completion-time bins are [start, end); only the last bin includes its upper endpoint. Final partial bins keep their actual widths and smaller samples. The last bin includes a short active tail before scheduling stops; it is not entirely drain. Missing latency and bins without completions leave gaps. Swipe plots on narrow screens, or focus and use arrow keys.</p>
<h3>Protected canary phase durations over time</h3>
<p>{{len .ExperienceCanaries}} cycles: {{len .Experience.canaries}} shared baseline; {{range .Experience.arms}}{{len .canaries}} steady at {{n .shares 0}} shares; {{end}}baseline observations appear once.</p>
{{if .ExperienceIncomplete}}<p class="annotation" role="status">Incomplete or failed canaries: {{range .ExperienceIncomplete}}{{.id}} ({{.status}}); {{end}}missing completion is not success. See phase evidence below.</p>{{end}}
<div class="experience-controls"><label><input id="experience-baseline-toggle" type="checkbox" checked> Show shared baseline</label><label><input id="experience-hard-toggle" type="checkbox"> Show recorded hard deadlines (rescale each phase)</label></div>
<figure><div id="experience-canaries" class="experience-plot" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Canary ACK, Ready and Cleanup durations, scroll horizontally"></div><figcaption>Three independent seconds axes keep ACK visible. All three phase observations use <strong>cycle preflight start</strong> as x, aligning the same operation, not stage completion time. Tooltips retain actual stage start/completion and recorded duration.</figcaption></figure>
<div class="experience-legend"><span>Hollow gray circles: shared baseline</span><span>Filled teal / periwinkle: steady arms</span><span>Orange ring: exceeds soft expectation</span><span>Orange short dash: soft expectation at this cycle</span><span>Gray dashed: hard deadline (optional)</span><span>Hollow cross: incomplete, elapsed/censored or unknown</span></div>
<p class="muted">Ready includes ACK; never add them. Cleanup includes watch setup. Soft expectations record degradation, not an abort or SLO; absent baseline expectations remain not evaluated. Hard deadlines are separate and hidden by default. Missing completion never becomes a zero-duration success. Censored elapsed values are not completed durations.</p>
<details {{if .ExperienceIncomplete}}open{{end}}><summary>Every canary cycle: actual phase values, soft expectations and hard deadlines</summary><div class="table-scroll"><table id="experience-cycle-table"><caption>Recorded seconds and actual source timestamps; cycle status is retained, not inferred from a soft threshold</caption><thead><tr><th>Cycle / phase / status</th><th>Stage</th><th>Start / completion (source timestamps)</th><th>Duration / elapsed (s)</th><th>Soft expected (s)</th><th>Hard deadline (s)</th></tr></thead><tbody>
{{range .ExperienceCanaries}}{{$cycle := .}}{{range $name, $stage := .stages}}<tr><th>{{$cycle.id}} / {{$cycle.phase}} / {{$cycle.status}}</th><td>{{$name}}{{if eq $name "ready"}} (includes ACK){{end}}</td><td>{{text $stage.startedRFC3339}}<br>{{text $stage.completedRFC3339}}</td><td>{{n $stage.durationSeconds 6}}{{if not (knownNumber $stage.completed)}} (elapsed/censored if recorded; not completed){{end}}</td><td>{{if knownNumber $stage.expectedSeconds}}{{n $stage.expectedSeconds 6}}{{else}}not evaluated{{end}}</td><td>{{n $stage.hardDeadlineSeconds 3}}</td></tr>{{end}}{{end}}
</tbody></table></div></details>
<details><summary>Experience method and source metadata (labels only; hashes not verified here)</summary><pre>{{pretty .Experience.method}}</pre><pre>{{pretty .Experience.sources}}</pre><ul>{{range .Experience.limitations}}<li>{{.}}</li>{{end}}</ul></details>
{{else}}<p class="empty">No experience time series supplied. Per-bin client behavior and canary phase timings are unknown. Supply --experience FILE to display reviewed observations; no raw artifacts are opened.</p>{{end}}
</section>
<style>
#experience{min-width:0}.experience-headlines{margin-bottom:20px}.experience-headlines h3{font-size:1.5rem}.experience-headlines small{font-size:.8rem;font-weight:400}.experience-plot{min-width:0;max-width:100%;overflow-x:auto;margin-bottom:8px}.experience-plot svg{display:block;width:100%;min-width:760px}.experience-plot svg text{font:11px system-ui;fill:var(--muted)}.experience-controls,.experience-legend{display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px 22px;margin:12px 0;font-size:.82rem}.experience-controls label{display:inline-flex;align-items:center;gap:8px;min-height:36px}.experience-controls input{width:18px;height:18px;accent-color:var(--teal)}.experience-plot:focus-visible,.experience-controls input:focus-visible{outline:3px solid var(--orange);outline-offset:2px}.experience-legend span{border-bottom:2px solid var(--line)}#experience>figure{margin-top:24px}#experience pre{max-height:28rem;overflow:auto}#experience-cycle-table th,#experience-cycle-table td{overflow-wrap:anywhere;min-width:100px}#experience-cycle-table td:nth-child(3){min-width:250px}
.experience-plot svg{min-width:900px}
</style>{{end}}`
